# PyInstaller build stack for `make desktop-package` (desktop-distribution-m7).
# DELIBERATELY outside pyproject.toml/uv.lock (MinerU precedent): build-only
# tooling must not enter the runtime wheel's resolvable dependency surface or
# perturb wheel-check. Pins mirror spike-1's measured toolchain
# (.claude/notes/spikes/desktop-distribution-spike-1.md:15). Regenerate the
# hashed lockfile after ANY edit here:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     apps/desktop/pyinstaller/requirements-build.in \
#     -o apps/desktop/pyinstaller/requirements-build.txt
# then verify the pyinstaller wheel hash still matches the spike pin
# (327d1323...) before committing, and re-run `make desktop-package-check`.
#
# SCOPE: macOS/Linux only. Resolved on macOS with no environment markers, so
# the lock pins darwin-only `macholib` and omits PyInstaller's Windows
# requirement `pywin32-ctypes`; `--require-hashes` then forbids resolving it
# at install time. Windows support means regenerating with `--universal` plus
# `sys_platform` markers AND deriving `_tool_env()["PATH"]` per-platform.
pyinstaller==6.21.0
pyinstaller-hooks-contrib==2026.6
